[2026-09-21 14:33:19 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 027]   Step_03 found the outer-comet perihelion anisotropy near
[2026-09-21 14:33:19 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 027]   lam ~ 219 deg and the detached-TNO cluster near lam ~ 49 deg --
[2026-09-21 14:33:19 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 027]   the two ends of ONE axis.  A directed field structure predicts
[2026-09-21 14:33:19 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 027]   exactly this bipolar pattern on different dynamical
[2026-09-21 14:33:19 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 027]   populations; a point mass does not.  But comet perihelion
[2026-09-21 14:33:19 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 027]   statistics are discovery-biased, so the JFC sample gets the
[2026-09-21 14:33:19 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 027]   full bias machinery developed for the TNOs:
[2026-09-21 14:33:19 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 027]   B1  Reconstruct the JFC discovery footprint (provisional
[2026-09-21 14:33:19 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 027]   designation -> lam_opp) and measure the realized coupling
[2026-09-21 14:33:19 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 027]   Delta = varpi - lam_opp.
[2026-09-21 14:33:19 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 027]   B2  The pairing test: if JFC varpi clustering were pure
[2026-09-21 14:33:19 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 027]   footprint smear, the observed (lam_opp, Delta) pairing is
[2026-09-21 14:33:19 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 027]   a typical shuffle of the marginals.  Under intrinsic
[2026-09-21 14:33:19 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 027]   clustering the pairing compensates -- same machinery as
[2026-09-21 14:33:19 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 027]   b8/D2.
[2026-09-21 14:33:19 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 027]   B3  Ceiling: R(varpi) vs R(lam_opp) -- can the realized
[2026-09-21 14:33:19 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 027]   footprint reach the observed concentration at all?
[2026-09-21 14:33:19 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 027]   B4  Era and quality stability: designation-era splits,
[2026-09-21 14:33:19 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 027]   and cross-checks in the CTc and HYP classes.
